WASTEPAY - PICKUP LOGISTICS


1. PURPOSE

The Pickup Logistics System exists to manage residential and institutional plastic collection operations through intelligent dispatching, vehicle management, route optimization, and depot reconciliation procedures.



--------------------------------------------------


2. VEHICLE FLEET MANAGEMENT

Every operational vehicle must maintain the following records:

- Vehicle License Plate
- Vehicle Capacity (KG or Tons)
- Assigned Depot
- Assigned Driver
- Current Operational Status

Business Rule:

Every collection vehicle must be assigned to a single active depot.



--------------------------------------------------


3. DRIVER SHIFT STATUS LIFECYCLE


OFFLINE

↓

AVAILABLE

↓

ON_ROUTE

↓

AT_PICKUP

↓

RETURNING_TO_DEPOT

↓

SHIFT_COMPLETED


Business Rule:

Only AVAILABLE drivers may receive new pickup assignments.



--------------------------------------------------


4. VEHICLE CAPACITY SAFEGUARDS

The system continuously tracks:

- Estimated route weight.
- Remaining vehicle capacity.
- Daily collection totals.

Business Rule:

If vehicle capacity exceeds 85%, additional pickups may not be assigned without manager approval.



--------------------------------------------------


5. DEPOT RESPONSIBILITY ZONES

WastePay utilizes PostGIS spatial mapping to define:

- Collection zones.
- Depot service areas.
- Geographic boundaries.

Business Rules:

- Pickup requests are routed exclusively to the nearest eligible depot.
- Depot Managers cannot accept out-of-zone requests.
- Requests outside service areas are automatically rejected.



--------------------------------------------------


6. ROUTE OPTIMIZATION ENGINE

The system is designed to optimize:

- Shortest route distance.
- Pickup sequencing.
- Vehicle capacity.
- Collection weight estimates.
- Depot proximity.

Future capabilities include:

- Traffic-aware routing.
- Intelligent dispatch recommendations.
- Dynamic route recalculation.



--------------------------------------------------


7. DRIVER LOCATION TRACKING

While actively on shift:

- Driver GPS coordinates are transmitted every three minutes.
- Depot Managers may view active driver locations.

Business Rule:

Location tracking is only enabled during active working hours.



--------------------------------------------------


8. NAVIGATION INTEGRATION

Drivers may launch navigation directly from the PWA.

Supported navigation applications include:

- Google Maps
- Waze

Navigation links are dynamically generated using customer GPS coordinates.



--------------------------------------------------


